lity":true,"_score_rev_volatility":100.0,"_gate_margin_vs_hist":-0.0045402455820447475,"_gp_margin_vs_hist":true,"_score_margin_vs_hist":100.0,"_gate_piotroski":7,"_gp_piotroski":true,"_score_piotroski":77.8,"_gate_spread":-0.035971201194009,"_gp_spread":false,"_score_spread":0.0,"_gate_roic_consistency":0.33409438386825385,"_gp_roic_consistency":false,"_score_roic_consistency":44.3,"_gate_incr_roic":-0.015806988352745424,"_gp_incr_roic":false,"_score_incr_roic":11.4,"_gate_margin_advantage":-0.07008995054957243,"_gp_margin_advantage":false,"_score_margin_advantage":10.0,"_gate_pool_share":0.06256055198635146,"_gp_pool_share":true,"_score_pool_share":65.0,"_gate_rev_durability":null,"_gp_rev_durability":null,"_score_rev_durability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":0.0,"_gate_fund_growth":0,"_gp_fund_growth":false,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.03238979695484085,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":47.1,"_gate_share_shrink":-0.0028648136199173058,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":53.6,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.0035665503111246017,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":94.1,"_gate_insider_own":0.01064,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":7.1,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"GXO Logistics, Inc., together with its subsidiaries, provides logistics services worldwide. It provides warehousing and distribution, order fulfilment, e-commerce, reverse logistics, and other supply chain services. As of December 31, 2025, it operated in 1,043 facilities. The company serves a range of customers in the e-commerce, omnichannel retail, technology and consumer electronics, food and beverage, industrial and manufacturing, consumer packaged goods, and other industries. GXO Logistics, Inc. was incorporated in 2021 and is headquartered in Greenwich, Connecticut.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Patrick  Kelleher | CEO & Director | Age 56 | Compensation: $1.1M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 150K people. Revenue per employee of $88K ranks in the bottom quartile among Industrials peers, with revenue growing 14%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $733 of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $313 per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 13\u00d7 revenue per employee (reasonable relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (9/10).","financial_summary":["GXO Logistics, Inc. is a mid-cap industrials business with a $6.2B market cap on $13.2B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +14% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 5% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $110M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 1 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 13.56\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 2.5\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and thin 1.8\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 3.2% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.2\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 49% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.4877112982568013},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.6) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 7.5% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Industrials sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 6% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cyclicality and capital intensity \u2014 order books turn on a dime, and the heavy fixed cost base that creates the moat also magnifies the downturn.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Supply chain reshoring costs and labour shortages \u2014 onshoring mandates raise capex requirements while a shrinking skilled-labour pool inflates operating costs.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Piotroski score 7/9 \u2014 financials improving across profitability, leverage and efficiency"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"GXO Doubles Down On Humanoids With Plan For Up To 1,000 Apptronik Robots","source":"forbes.com","link":"https://www.forbes.com/sites/johnkoetsier/2026/11/12/gxo-doubles-down-on-humanoids-with-plan-for-up-to-1000-apptronik-robots/","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794488079.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"GXO and Apptronik Expand Partnership to Scale Humanoid Deployment","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/technology/ai/articles/gxo-apptronik-expand-partnership-scale-120000586.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794484800.0,"origin":"t